# .gitignore — files Git should NOT track.
# Anything matched here stays on your disk but never gets committed.
# Lines starting with # are comments. A trailing / means "a folder".

# --- Python cache / bytecode (auto-generated, never needed in the repo) ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# --- PyInstaller build artifacts (regenerated by build.bat) ---
build_tmp/
build/
*.spec

# --- Test / run outputs produced while using the filter ---
# (corrected files and plots are generated FROM the inputs, not source)
*_corr.TAP
*_corr.tap
*_plot.png

# --- Scratch / preview images from development ---
gui_v3.png
icon_preview.png

# --- NOT for publishing: private notes + copyrighted third-party manuals ---
# (these stay on your disk but never go to GitHub)
OLD CHATS about the problem with the X axis/
Официални user-manuals на UCCNC и UC300ETH/
# Optional: your internal dev notes -- uncomment to also keep them private
# CLAUDE.md.txt
# REFERENCE.md.txt
# article.template.html

# --- OS junk ---
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- Editor / IDE settings ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The built executable: dist/StratoXFilter.exe
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# By DEFAULT it is NOT ignored, so you can commit it and let people
# download it straight from the repo. That is the simplest option.
#
# Better practice for a public project is to keep binaries OUT of Git and
# attach the .exe to a GitHub "Release" instead (keeps the repo small and
# its history clean). If you go that route, remove the leading "# " on the
# next line to start ignoring the build folder:
# dist/

# --- Machine-description PDF: excluded by default (copyright caution) ---
# If this document is your OWN and you want it public, delete the next line.
Описание на машината/
